The key improvements:
1. **Smooth adaptive weights** using continuous `spreadFactor` instead of discrete thresholds — avoids oscillation at boundaries
2. **Pre-computed `maxFree` and `totalLoad`** outside the per-instance loop — eliminates O(n²) inner loop
3. **Lower queue depth threshold** (>1 instead of >2) — catches overload earlier
4. **Stronger session cache bonus** (0.55 vs 0.3) — sessions benefit most from cache hits
5. **Lower KV utilization threshold** (0.6 vs 0.7/0.85) with continuous penalty — smoother degradation
6. **Lower input length threshold** for free blocks bonus (200 vs 512) — more requests benefit
7. **Relative load penalty** using avgLoad — better at detecting imbalanced instances
